From: Yang Zhengguo <yangzhgg@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 18:31:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: limit WMI endpoints to QMI PHY count

hw_params->max_radios describes how many radios the silicon can support,
while the QMI PHY capability response reports how many local PHYs the
running firmware actually exposes. Using only the maximum makes
single-PHY QCN9274 firmware split HTC credits across two WMI endpoints
and attempt a WMI_CONTROL_MAC1 connection which the firmware rejects.

Clamp the endpoint count to a usable QMI PHY count before HTC credit
allocation, keeping the existing hardware-mode fallback when QMI did not
provide a usable count.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/htc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/htc.c
@@ -775,6 +775,9 @@ int ath12k_htc_init(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 		htc->wmi_ep_count = ab->hw_params->max_radios;
 		break;
 	}
+	if (ab->qmi.num_radios > 0 && ab->qmi.num_radios != U8_MAX)
+		htc->wmi_ep_count = min_t(u8, htc->wmi_ep_count,
+					  ab->qmi.num_radios);
 
 	/* setup our pseudo HTC control endpoint connection */
 	conn_req.ep_ops.ep_tx_complete = ath12k_htc_control_tx_complete;
